From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 08:05:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: Retry transient MHI suspend busy on PEACH

The MHI host can temporarily reject suspend while a client still
holds a device wake reference or a packet is pending. Its -EBUSY
return precedes the M3 request, so those cases can be retried without
overlapping an in-progress state transition.

Match the original Piano CNSS driver. For PEACH, allow up to three
additional attempts spaced 5 to 6 milliseconds apart. Return the
first error other than -EBUSY immediately since an error can follow
the M3 request. Keep the existing policy for other hardware.

Codex checked the original CNSS control flow and the Linux MHI error
paths, then verified the retry counts, early errors and PEACH scope
with ARM64 Kbuild and eight source-based tests.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
index 1b8d47e..fd9d02d 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
  * Copyright (c) Qualcomm Technologies, Inc. and/or its subsidiaries.
  */
 
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/msi.h>
 #include <linux/pci.h>
 #include <linux/firmware.h>
@@ -14,6 +15,7 @@
 #include "pci.h"
 
 #define MHI_TIMEOUT_DEFAULT_MS	90000
+#define ATH12K_PEACH_MHI_SUSPEND_RETRIES	3
 #define OTP_INVALID_BOARD_ID	0xFFFF
 #define OTP_VALID_DUALMAC_BOARD_ID_MASK		0x1000
 #define MHI_CB_INVALID	0xff
@@ -415,6 +417,26 @@ static int ath12k_mhi_check_state_bit(struct ath12k_pci *ab_pci,
 	return -EINVAL;
 }
 
+static int ath12k_mhi_pm_suspend(struct ath12k_pci *ab_pci)
+{
+	struct mhi_controller *mhi = ab_pci->mhi_ctrl;
+	int retries = 0;
+	int ret;
+
+	if (ab_pci->ab->hw_rev == ATH12K_HW_PEACH_HW20)
+		retries = ATH12K_PEACH_MHI_SUSPEND_RETRIES;
+
+	ret = mhi_pm_suspend(mhi);
+	/* A busy return precedes the M3 request. Let in-flight work drain. */
+	while (ret == -EBUSY && retries > 0) {
+		retries--;
+		usleep_range(5000, 6000);
+		ret = mhi_pm_suspend(mhi);
+	}
+
+	return ret;
+}
+
 static int ath12k_mhi_set_state(struct ath12k_pci *ab_pci,
 				enum ath12k_mhi_state mhi_state)
 {
@@ -463,7 +485,7 @@ static int ath12k_mhi_set_state(struct ath12k_pci *ab_pci,
 		ret = 0;
 		break;
 	case ATH12K_MHI_SUSPEND:
-		ret = mhi_pm_suspend(ab_pci->mhi_ctrl);
+		ret = ath12k_mhi_pm_suspend(ab_pci);
 		break;
 	case ATH12K_MHI_RESUME:
 		ret = mhi_pm_resume(ab_pci->mhi_ctrl);
-- 
